# Engineering Core

Apply to every engineering task. The full text is in the skills `ub-engineering`,
`ub-workflow`, and `ub-quality-gates` (`.cursor/skills/` or `~/.cursor/skills/`);
read them at the start of a task.

- **Attack the premise.** After two failed fixes of the same problem, stop
  patching. List the assumptions of the approach and test the weakest one.
- **Test behavior, not implementation.** Assert what a caller observes. Derive
  expected values from the requirement, never from the code's current output.
- **Subtract before you add.** Try deleting or simplifying before adding a class,
  abstraction, option, or dependency. Make the smallest change that solves the task.
- **TDD by default.** Failing test first for behavior changes and bug fixes; no
  artificial tests for trivial changes.
- **Root cause.** Reproduce, explain the mechanism, then fix the cause.
- **Evidence before claims.** Report only what you verified by running a check.
- **Quality gates** are proportionate to risk and use only installed tools.
  Metrics (coverage, CRAP < 10, duplication) are indicators, not proof.
- **Git safety.** Commit only on request. Push only with explicit permission.
  Never delete user work, branches, worktrees, or untracked files automatically.
- **User skills.** For every task, engineering or not, load and apply: <!-- kit:user-skills -->none installed<!-- /kit:user-skills -->
  (from `<!-- kit:user-skills-dir -->~/ai/user-skills/<!-- /kit:user-skills-dir -->`).
- **Skill tiers.** Core always; language skills by project language and task;
  technology skills only when the technology is used in the project.
- **Comment language.** Match the file (English → English, Russian → Russian);
  mixed about equally → Russian; none → neighboring files, else Russian. Do not
  mass-translate existing comments. Never use the letter «ё» in comments;
  write «е» instead. No period at the end of a sentence or paragraph when
  nothing or only a blank line follows it; periods between sentences stay.
